Print-shop specifications change
--------------------------------
The print geometry in this toolkit (trim, bleed, spine width, full-wrap cover
panels) is tuned to one shop and one size (Blurb Large-Square 12×12 in) as a
worked reference. PRINT SHOPS CHANGE THEIR TEMPLATES WITHOUT NOTICE. Before you
order, ALWAYS re-verify the current template with your shop's own live
PDF-to-Book calculator, and date-stamp any spec you record. See
docs/PRINT_RUNBOOK.md.

Third-party components
----------------------
This project depends on third-party software, each under its own license. It
does NOT bundle or relicense any of them — you install them yourself:

- Pillow, pillow-heif, rawpy, imagehash, piexif, NumPy, pandas, PyYAML, click
  — installed via pip (see requirements.txt); each retains its own license.
- OpenCV (opencv-python-headless) — includes the Haar cascade classifiers used
  by the gutter/face scan; under its own (Apache-2.0) license.
- Playwright + Chromium — installed via `playwright install chromium`.

Real-ESRGAN (OPTIONAL, not included)
------------------------------------
The optional GPU upscaler (scripts/upscale_batch.py) drives the third-party
`realesrgan-ncnn-vulkan` binary. That binary is NOT bundled with this project —
it is a ~45MB download with its own license and attribution requirements.
Download it yourself from the upstream Real-ESRGAN project and comply with its
license. The reliable default path in this toolkit uses CPU Lanczos and requires
no external binary (see docs/UPSCALING.md).

Fonts
-----
The exporter uses whatever serif/sans fonts it can find on your system (or the
ones you point it at via PHOTOBOOK_FONT_SERIF / PHOTOBOOK_FONT_SANS). No fonts
are bundled; each font on your machine retains its own license.
